  "id": "Compound::DB00398 - Gene::5243",
  "verbalization": "Sorafenib is implicated in the regulation of Abcb1 through multiple mechanistic pathways, primarily involving the binding of specific compounds to this transporter. The evidence suggests that Sorafenib may act as a causal agent in the upregulation of Abcb1, as it is linked to conditions such as International Normalised Ratio Abnormal, Tumour Pain, and Blood Thyroid Stimulating Hormone Increased, all of which are associated with the binding of Lomitapide or Vinorelbine to Abcb1. These compounds, in turn, bind to Abcb1, indicating a potential role for Sorafenib in modulating its expression through a shared pathway involving organonitrogen compounds. The integration of these pathways highlights a recurring mechanism where Sorafenib may influence Abcb1 through the interaction with compounds that bind to it, potentially affecting drug efflux and cellular drug resistance. The evidence is supported by the presence of a common ancestor in the pathway, reinforcing the connectivity between Sorafenib and Abcb1 through the binding of related compounds.",
